  "diagnosis": {
    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 0.75,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.1,
    "rationale": "The abrupt plateau at ~0.73 right after exponential growth could mean the reader was saturating, so I tested linearity with dilutions of the retained plateau aliquots. 18 h at 10x: 0.0763, 0.0770 → ×10 = 0.766. 18 h at 4x: 0.182, 0.190 → ×4 = 0.744. 12 h at 10x: 0.0724, 0.0785 → ×10 = 0.755. The undiluted readings were 0.728 (18 h) and 0.736 (12 h). Across dilutions of 1x, 4x and 10x, the back-calculated OD stays within about 3–5% of the undiluted value. That small difference is close to replicate scatter, and it does not grow with dilution the way detector saturation would make it. So the reader is effectively linear here, and the plateau is a real stationary phase. Biomass over the final hours is as read, at about 0.73–0.77 (best estimate about 0.75)."
  },
